1.1 Definitions

Unless the context otherwise requires, the following terms shall have the meanings assigned to them below:

- "**Annette L. Godfrey’s** Account" means the account held by **Annette L. Godfrey** with the Clearing House;
- "**Clearing House”** means the central clearinghouse designated by the Parties for the Clearing of Transactions;
- "**Clearing”** means the process of transmitting, reconciling, and, where appropriate, confirming Transactions for clearing and settlement through the Clearing House;
- "**Transaction**" means any over-the-counter derivative transaction entered into between the Parties, the terms of which are governed by this Clearing Protocol;
- "**Effective Date**" means **10 Mar 82 13:57:28** (UTC), being the date and time of the first Transaction;
- “**Parties**” means each of the counterparties to a Transaction;
- “**Settlement Amount**” means the amount payable by one Party to the other in respect of a Transaction;
- “**Settlement Date**” means the date on which a Settlement Amount is due to be paid;
- “**Settlement Obligation**” means the obligation of a Party to pay a Settlement Amount to the other Party on the Settlement Date;
- “**Settlement Obligation**” means the obligation of a Party to pay a Settlement Amount to the other Party on the Settlement Date;
- “**Settlement Instructions**” means the instructions provided by the Parties to the Clearing House for the purpose of settling a Transaction;
- “**Settlement Message**” means a message sent by the Clearing House to the Parties in accordance with the Settlement Instructions;
- “**Settlement**” means the process of exchanging value between the Parties in accordance with the Settlement Instructions;

1.2 Governing Law

This Clearing Protocol shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of **New York**.

